# Strict Type Checking
RULE: Use TypedDict, Protocol, TypeVar, type aliases — avoid Any. Only audited bypasses in QUALITY_GATE_BYPASS_AUDIT.md may pass.
WHY: Any defeats type safety, autocomplete, refactoring; reportAny is BLOCKING in quality gates.
CODEX: 06-coding-standards/README.md#type-hints, .cursor/rules/no-type-any-use-specific.mdc
DO: Use `dict[str, str]`; Protocol for duck typing; TypeVar for generics; TypedDict for known keys
NEVER: Use Any without justification; relax reportAny; add baseline files
